[I] Firewall configuration tool

[T] ferm is a frontend for iptables that reads firewall rules from a
[T] structured configuration file and calls iptables to insert them into the
[T] running kernel. It aims to make rules easy to write and read, with
[T] support for variables, functions and arrays.

[U] http://ferm.foo-projects.org/

[A] Ferm Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

